1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:12,440
Molly, I need your special talent for handling special matters.

2
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:15,400
Like what special matters?

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,630
Well, I have a scheduling problem.

4
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:18,710
Yes?

5
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:22,160
I have three tonsillectomies set for Friday with Dr. Earl.

6
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:23,330
Yes?

7
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:26,820
I need to fit a fourth operation into his schedule.

8
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:30,680
And ... I know you can do it.

9
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,140
Who's the patient?

10
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,180
Carl Herrera.

11
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:34,740
The boy has infected tonsils,

12
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:37,640
and we should remove them as soon as possible.

13
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,410
Well, I'll try to arrange the schedule, Dr. Stewart.

14
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:43,040
But it's not going to be easy.

15
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:47,940
I know you'll be able to take care of it.

16
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:49,360
Well, Mrs. Herrera,

17
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:53,250
Carl will be perfectly fine after we remove his tonsils.

18
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:55,810
Thank you for your reassurance, Dr. Stewart.

19
00:00:55,810 --> 00:00:58,820
He's had so many colds and sore throats recently.

20
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:01,260
Well, it's a very easy operation, Carl.

21
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:02,700
You won't feel a thing.

22
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:05,130
But when do they do it?

23
00:01:05,130 --> 00:01:06,620
This Friday.

24
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:09,960
But Saturday's my birthday.

25
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:14,670
Well, we could reschedule the operation, Mrs. Herrera,

26
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:17,290
but I don't want to put it off too long.

27
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:20,390
No, I think it's important to do it now.

28
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:22,190
We can have a birthday party for you, Carl,

29
00:01:22,190 --> 00:01:23,690
When you come out of the hospital.

30
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:26,240
But it won't be on my birthday.

31
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:29,520
But your health is more important, Carl. Believe me.

32
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:35,240
I don't want my tonsils out.

33
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:41,900
Nurse Baker, would you come in, please?

34
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:47,590
Hello, Mrs. Herrera. Hi, Carl, how you doing?

35
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:51,120
I don't want my tonsils out.

36
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,120
Come with me, Carl.

37
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:59,340
You and I will talk this over.

38
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:01,480
She has a special way with kids.

39
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:05,660
She sure does.

40
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:08,390
Carl, does your throat hurt?

41
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:09,570
Yes.

42
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:12,150
OK. Do you want to get better?

43
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:12,940
Yes.

44
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:15,750
OK. We want you to get better, too.

45
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:17,990
You'll have your tonsils out tomorrow,

46
00:02:17,990 --> 00:02:20,100
and you won't get so many colds anymore.

47
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:22,700
But if I have my tonsils out tomorrow,

48
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:25,890
I'll miss my birthday party on Saturday.

49
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:27,190
I know.

50
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:29,650
It's a problem, isn't it?

51
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:32,640
Let me try to work something out.

52
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:34,510
What?

53
00:02:34,510 --> 00:02:36,150
I have to think about it.

54
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:37,750
You're fooling me.

55
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:39,740
Oh, I'm not, Carl.

56
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,750
Give me a chance to think about it,

57
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:44,120
and I'll come up with something.

58
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:45,420
A surprise?

59
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:46,270
Maybe.

60
00:02:46,270 --> 00:02:48,190
But you just put on your pajamas and robe,

61
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:51,060
and I'll think of a surprise.

62
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,170
Will it hurt?

63
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:52,990
No.

64
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:54,400
There are other boys and girls here,

65
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,730
and they're having their tonsils out.

66
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:56,810
You'll meet them.

67
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:59,830
I don't want to.

68
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:01,450
Change your clothes, Carl.

69
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:04,450
Everything will be just fine.
